---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/bachelor-project.css';
---

<Layout>
  <main class="bachelor-page">

    <section class="bachelor-hero">
      <div class="bachelor-heading">
        <a class="back-link" href="/projects">← Projects</a>

        <p class="bachelor-label">
          03 · Chalmers · Networking · Software development
        </p>

        <h1 class="bachelor-title">
          Bachelor<br />
          Project
        </h1>

        <p class="bachelor-intro">
          A six-person Chalmers project exploring a network-driven approach
          to detecting when shared computers stop reporting.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bachelor-meta">
        <div>
          <span>Context</span>
          <strong>Chalmers University of Technology</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Team</span>
          <strong>Six-person group project</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Focus</span>
          <strong>Networking · Backend · Monitoring</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="story-section">
      <div class="story-heading">
        <span>Problem</span>

        <h2>
          When a computer<br />
          stops reporting.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p>
          Shared computers can be spread across several locations, making it
          difficult to notice quickly when one is disconnected or stolen.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our group explored whether network discovery and heartbeat signals could
          provide an early indication that a computer had disappeared. A missing heartbeat could
          flag a device for investigation, but could not determine why it had stopped reporting.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="system-section">
      <div class="system-heading">
        <span>System concept</span>

        <h2>
          Tracking devices<br />
          through heartbeats.
        </h2>

        <p>
          The prototype combined network discovery with a lightweight client
          that sent heartbeat signals to a central backend. The backend used
          them to track which known devices were reporting and flag those that stopped.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="system-flow">

        <div class="system-node">
          <span class="node-number">01</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Shared computer</strong>
            <p>Monitored endpoint</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="system-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="system-node system-node-accent">
          <span class="node-number">02</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Heartbeat client</strong>
            <p>Go · scheduled execution</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="system-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="system-node">
          <span class="node-number">03</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Backend</strong>
            <p>Spring Boot · device state</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="system-connector system-connector-alert" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="system-node system-node-alert">
          <span class="node-number">04</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Missing heartbeat</strong>
            <p>Flagged for investigation</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="contribution-section">
      <div class="contribution-heading">
        <span>My contribution</span>

        <h2>
          Backend, heartbeats<br />
          and documentation.
        </h2>

        <p>
          I worked on the backend and heartbeat mechanism, helped coordinate
          the early stages of the project and contributed to writing and editing the report.
          The system itself was designed and built by the six-person team.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="contribution-grid">

        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Backend development</h3>
          <p>
            Contributed to backend functionality for handling monitored
            devices and their stored state.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Heartbeat mechanism</h3>
          <p>
            Worked on the mechanism used to determine whether monitored
            computers were still reporting to the system.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Project coordination</h3>
          <p>
            Helped coordinate the early stages of the project and took part
            in technical discussions and decisions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Report editing</h3>
          <p>
            Contributed to writing and editing the group report, including
            editorial work across the document.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="technology-section">
      <div class="technology-heading">
        <span>Technology</span>

        <h2>
          Tools used<br />
          in the prototype.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="technology-list">

        <div>
          <span>Client</span>
          <strong>Go</strong>
          <p>Client for sending heartbeat signals from monitored computers.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Backend</span>
          <strong>Java · Spring Boot</strong>
          <p>Application logic and central handling of device information.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Data</span>
          <strong>H2 · JdbcTemplate</strong>
          <p>Persistence and database access during development.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Network</span>
          <strong>Nmap</strong>
          <p>Discovering devices on the network.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Endpoint</span>
          <strong>Windows Task Scheduler</strong>
          <p>Running the heartbeat client automatically on monitored systems.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="lesson-section">
      <div class="lesson-heading">
        <span>What I took from it</span>

        <h2>
          Building one system<br />
          as a team.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="lesson-copy">
        <p>
          The project gave me practical experience with networking and backend
          development, but also with taking a problem through research and design to a
          working prototype.
        </p>

        <p>
          Working as a team meant bringing together code, ideas
          and decisions from different parts of the project, then testing
          the result and documenting it in a shared report.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="bachelor-closing">
      <span>Chalmers · 2025</span>

      <p>
        Researched, designed and built collaboratively by the project team.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
